WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.051
01 / Establish a healthy baseline
Two healthy containers and a real customer request returning HTTP 200.

2
00:00:07.051 --> 00:00:15.769
02 / Introduce the bad port
The override changes CATALOG_URL to catalog:9090. The HTML page still loads; the customer request fails.

3
00:00:15.769 --> 00:00:35.681
03 / Diagnose from evidence
ECONNREFUSED points to catalog:9090. The same container can reach catalog:8081: the configured port is wrong.

4
00:00:35.681 --> 00:00:57.097
04 / Repair and verify Docker
Recreate with the known-good configuration. Check readiness, three customer requests, and their fresh logs.

5
00:00:57.097 --> 00:01:04.334
05 / Establish the Kubernetes baseline
The image is loaded into kind. Both Pods are ready; a request through the storefront Service succeeds.

6
00:01:04.334 --> 00:01:40.526
06 / Diagnose the unready Pod
The bad ConfigMap takes effect after replacement. Running with 0/1 ready and zero restarts is a readiness failure.

7
00:01:40.526 --> 00:02:09.560
07 / Repair and verify Kubernetes
Restore the ConfigMap and replace the Pod. Readiness, Service traffic, and fresh request logs now agree.
